-- examples/checks/agg-datastrat-elems.rofl — A RULE OF TWO ELEMENTS, the second grouped: both(T, S, B, N) has a sum keyed by T and a count whose group B no
-- premise binds. An instance the sum releases is read by the count under the rule's own reading, not under the
-- group the count's own firing binds, so each element fires the instances it reads and none is left to another.

edb(reports). edb(w). edb(top).
reports(b1, a). reports(b2, a). reports(c1, b1). reports(d1, c1).
w(b1, 5). w(b2, 7). w(c1, 2). w(d1, 1).
top(c1). top(a).
under(B, E) :- reports(E, B).
under(B, E) :- reports(M, B), both(c1, _, M, N), N >= 1, reports(E, M).
both(T, S, B, N) :- top(T), S is sum(V ; F : under(T, F), w(F, V)), N is count(E : under(B, E)).
